\title{A derived rule per projection chain and instance could recover 5 to 10 percent of the steps on Mathlib, exactly}
\taxon{Hypothesis}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\tag{soundness}
\meta{origin}{docs/design/review/exact-proof-conversion.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: [rep-exact-proof-conversion](rep-exact-proof-conversion), section 3.4; [the profiling session](ses-JRSD). Not built and not measured: the figure is the estimate of the author of that report, and the conditions were worked out on paper.}
\ul{
\li{The idea is the one official-exact route left open by [the search for a cheap exact proof comparison](ins-FIXO). For a partial application such as \code{\verb~|HMul.hMul A A A (instHMul A m)~}, remember that applied to two arguments it reaches the field of the weak-head normal form of \code{\verb~|m~}, and build that directly: one application instead of two unfoldings, two reductions, two applications and four records per side.}
\li{Four conditions make firing the rule on both sides the official outcome: every head of the chain is an abbreviation or opaque, never regular, and none is a Nat function; both sides fire rules with the same sequence of heads; the intermediate values that the official algorithm passes are known not to be proofs without building them; the intermediate quick tests can only answer true.}
\li{Size: bounded by the reduction share of the heavy units, 61 percent of the steps of the traced unit. The two-level chains of multiplication and addition are 1,920 of the 5,359 unfoldings of that unit; halving their cost is about a fifth of its steps. On Mathlib as a whole the estimate is 5 to 10 percent of the steps and less in CPU time.}
\li{It is the derived-rule mechanism of the machine, keyed additionally by the instance arguments and fired in lockstep inside lazy delta. That mechanism in its present form produced a wrong accept against the official checker in the adversarial review and stays off.}
}
\p{The prize is a tenth of [what the shortcuts remove](ins-HPBW). It would need an exactness review of the four conditions before it could be switched on.}
\p{See also: [the decision that derived rules stay off](dec-MOCU); [conversion](design-conversion).}
